#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""atlassian -- streamlined Atlassian Cloud CLI (Jira + Confluence) for skills and humans.

A single self-contained, stdlib-only tool. See README.md for the usage contract.
Run `atlassian`, `jira`, `confluence`, or `<any> <command> --help` for help.

Multi-call: invoked as `jira ...` it runs the jira group; as `confluence ...` the
confluence group; as `atlassian ...` the full surface. (argv[0] basename dispatch.)

Design notes for maintainers:
  - Auth: Atlassian API token + HTTP Basic (email:token). One token covers Jira and
    Confluence. The claude.ai Atlassian connector uses hosted OAuth a CLI cannot reuse.
  - TLS: some Python builds (python.org macOS framework builds) ship an EMPTY CA trust
    store, so HTTPS fails with CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED regardless of any sandbox.
    build_ssl_context() resolves a CA bundle at runtime (env -> certifi -> cached ->
    macOS keychain, in-memory) so it works even where the config dir is not writable.
  - Jira reads/search use REST v3; writes wrap plain text into ADF (v3 requires it).
  - Confluence uses REST v2 for pages (body-format atlas_doc_format, falling back to
    storage/XHTML) and v1 /wiki/rest/api/search for CQL.
  - Output favors compact text to keep token cost low; --json / --raw are escape hatches.
    Confluence page bodies are truncated by default (--full to opt out).
"""
